  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Bangladeshis are Muslim and carry Arabic or Persian origin names with a Bengali flavour, often after a Md. (Mohammad) prefix for men, as in Md. Tanvir Hossain. The last name is a family or title name (Rahman, Hossain, Chowdhury, Talukder) but many families do not share one: a son may take part of his father's name instead. Women often carry Akter, Khatun or Begum as their last name, or take the husband's name after marriage. Hindu families use Bengali names with family names like Das, Saha, Ghosh or Roy. Almost everyone also has a daak naam, a short pet name used by family and friends (Rony, Mitu, Shanto), which is what you hear on the street.",
